---
import brand from '@arcvia/brand'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base title="About us" description={`About ${brand.legalName}.`}>
  <section class="shell max-w-3xl py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="h2 mt-3 text-balance">
      Drawings are precise. What people picture from them is not.
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Every construction project runs on documents that only a trained reader
        can decode. The architect sees the finished building. The client sees
        lines. The gap between those two pictures is where revisions, delays and
        arguments come from.
      </p>
      <p>
        {brand.name} closes that gap. Upload the drawing you already have and get
        back a space anyone can walk through — on a laptop, a phone, or a
        headset — and change while they are standing in it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We build for the people doing the work: architects who need to present
        without hiring a visualisation studio, developers who need to sell before
        the foundation is poured, and construction teams who need everyone
        looking at the same thing.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-card border border-line bg-surface-alt p-8">
      <h2 class="h3">Free while we are in beta</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        We would rather have the product in real projects than behind a paywall.
        Every account gets everything, including GPU renders, at no cost. When we
        do introduce paid plans you will hear about it well in advance.
      </p>
      <a href="/register/" class="btn-primary mt-6">Create an account</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
